  "title": "Global Markets Comment: Distinguishing AI Risks\u2014Size of the Pie vs. Share of the Pie",
  "type": "macro",
  "priority": "high",
  "published": "2026-07-24",
  "insights": [
   "Investors should distinguish between 'aggregate' shocks (size of the pie) and 'distributional' shocks (share of the pie) when assessing risks to AI-related equities.",
   "Aggregate shocks, such as macro headwinds or broad AI adoption concerns, have reliable cross-asset impacts, typically pushing equity indices lower and affecting rates, while distributional shocks have limited impact on broad indices.",
   "The market is currently vulnerable to challenges to the optimistic AI story, as valuations now require more optimistic assumptions about the Present Discounted Value (PDV) of economic gains.",
   "Macro hedges are effective against aggregate shocks, but hedging distributional shocks is more challenging as they often have offsetting effects at the macro level.",
   "Recent volatility in AI-related equities has been driven largely by distributional concerns, except during specific macro events like the Iran War."
